## 1. Summary

The Evolve LLM proxy writes one usage row per proxied completion, which is correct. But it derives the row's identity from the **run** (`invocationId: evolve:<runId>`) while holding `attemptIndex` at a constant `0`. The ledger's idempotency key is `(sessionId, invocationId, invocationKind, attemptIndex)`, so for a run that makes N model calls the first row is written and calls 2..N are discarded as if they were replays of call 1. Nothing is logged on that path, so the loss is invisible.

Measured on a real environment: a 73-call research recorded **0.83 %** of its tokens, and an 85-call research recorded **0.93 %**.

## 2. Expected behaviour

The repository already pins this contract in its own tests. `(invocationId, attemptIndex)` is the **attempt axis of one logical call**, not the identity of a run:

```ts
// services/api/src/store.test.ts:1184
test("SessionStore ignores duplicate model usage attempts but keeps retries", …
// :1220  await store.appendModelInvocationUsage(record);
// :1221  await store.appendModelInvocationUsage({ …record, id: "usage-duplicate", totalTokens: 30 });
// :1222  await store.appendModelInvocationUsage({ …record, attemptIndex: 1, id: "usage-retry", totalTokens: 4 });
// :1225  assert.deepEqual(records.map((usage) => usage.id).toSorted(), ["usage-0", "usage-retry"]);
// :1226  assert.deepEqual(records.map((usage) => usage.attemptIndex).toSorted(), [0, 1]);

// services/api/src/model-usage.test.ts:83
test("USG-005 invocation attempts keep a stable invocationId and increment attemptIndex", …
```

So: two rows that share all four key fields **must** be the same attempt of the same call, and a genuinely new call must present either a new `invocationId` or a higher `attemptIndex`. Distinct calls that differ only in their row `id` (`:259`, `randomBytes(16)`) are, by this contract, not distinguishable.

The same file already contains a writer that satisfies the contract for the very same `invocationKind`:

```ts
// services/api/src/evolution/direction-draft.ts:58-63
const id = randomUUID();
await store.appendModelInvocationUsage({
  id, invocationId: id, invocationKind: "evolve", attemptIndex: 0,
  outcome: draft ? "completed" : "failed", …
```

## 3. Actual behaviour

One row per run. Everything after the first completion is dropped in silence.

## 4. Source code

All paths relative to the repository root, quoted at main `f0efd382e`.

### 4.1 The writer builds a run-scoped key with a constant attempt index

```ts
// services/api/src/evolution/llm-proxy.ts
:232    try {
:233      const usage = await recordUsage(deps, grant, model, payload, startedAt);
:234      deps.onUsage?.(usage);
:235    } catch (error) {
:236      apiLog.warn("evolve_llm_usage_unrecorded", {          // only fires on a thrown error
:245  async function recordUsage(
:252    const reported = parseProviderUsage(payload.usage, "openai-chat-completions");
:253    const record: ModelInvocationUsage = {
:254      attemptIndex: 0,                                      // constant for every call of the run
:259      id: randomBytes(16).toString("hex"),                  // unique row id — not part of the key
:261      invocationId: `evolve:${grant.runId}`,                // one key per run
:264      invocationKind: "evolve",
:277    await deps.store.appendModelInvocationUsage(record);
```

### 4.2 The ledger drops the second call without a trace

```ts
// services/api/src/store.ts
:7634   async appendModelInvocationUsage(usage: ModelInvocationUsage): Promise<void> {
:7640     if (records.some((record) =>
:7641       record.sessionId === usage.sessionId
:7642       && record.invocationId === usage.invocationId
:7643       && record.invocationKind === usage.invocationKind
:7644       && record.attemptIndex === usage.attemptIndex)) {
:7645       return;                                            // silent: no log, no counter, no signal
:7647     records.push(this.normalizeModelInvocationUsage(usage));
:7652   async getSessionUsageSummary(sessionId: string) { … }  // summariseModelUsage counts rows as calls
```

The early `return` at `:7645` is not an error, so `llm-proxy.ts:236`'s `evolve_llm_usage_unrecorded` warning cannot fire for the calls this drops.

## 5. Reproduction

### 5.1 Observed on a real run (read-only inspection of an existing data volume)

Environment: a running ScienceDiscovery stack, Evolve search driven through the normal `/idea-tree` research path, one session, provider usage reported on every call.

| Evolve run | Proxied calls (proxy log) | Σ tokens at the proxy | Ledger rows for that `runId` | Tokens in the ledger | Share recorded |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `research-2864a8e9-ab07-4c8a-9d33-0be6f17639c3` | 73 (73 × HTTP 200, 0 non-200) | 1,752,397 (in 1,282,961 / out 469,436) | **1** | 14,621 | **0.8343 %** |
| `research-4f368ef0-e973-4b88-8806-72b2b53a0967` | 85 (85 × HTTP 200, 0 non-200) | 1,665,891 (in 1,140,337 / out 525,554) | **1** | 15,545 | **0.9331 %** |

Additional readings from the same pass:

- Each surviving row's `totalTokens` equals the **first** proxied call's total, and its `startedAt`/`finishedAt` bracket only that first call — the row kept is call 1, not an aggregate.
- `invocationKind` census of the whole ledger: 7 rows total — 5 `task`, 2 `evolve`.
- **Distinct dedup keys in the ledger: 7. Keys holding more than one row: 0.** Under this key a second row for the same run can never be written — the loss is structural, not a race.
- The engine's own state file self-reports `tokens = 1,752,397` and `1,665,891`, matching the proxy sums exactly: the spend is real and known to the engine; only the ledger is short.

### 5.2 Deterministic unit reproduction (specified, **not executed** in this pass)

No model or agent run is needed:

```ts
const key = { sessionId, invocationKind: "evolve", attemptIndex: 0 };
await store.appendModelInvocationUsage({ …key, id: "call-1", invocationId: "evolve:research-x", inputTokens: 9883, outputTokens: 4738, totalTokens: 14621 });
await store.appendModelInvocationUsage({ …key, id: "call-2", invocationId: "evolve:research-x", inputTokens: 12000, outputTokens: 6000, totalTokens: 18000 });
// Assert what §2's contract requires: two rows, one per call.
// Actual: listModelInvocationUsage returns 1 row (14,621) and the second append returns silently.
```

## 6. Scientific impact

1. **Cost of a research run is understated by two orders of magnitude.** An autonomous idea-tree search recorded 0.83 % and 0.93 % of what it spent. Any budget decision, quota, or "is this worth re-running" judgement made from `/api/sessions/{id}/usage` or the usage page is made against a number that is ~1/100 of reality.
2. **The direction of the error is silently wrong, not merely coarse.** `usageStatus: "reported"` on the surviving row asserts provider figures were captured. The row is not "an estimate" — it is call 1, labelled as the run.
3. **Per-call attribution is unrecoverable from the ledger.** Which round/candidate a token figure belongs to cannot be reconstructed, so a search cannot be compared to a cheaper alternative search on cost, and cost-per-insight cannot be computed at all.
4. **Nothing surfaces the loss.** The silent `return` produces no log line, and the only warning on this path is gated on an exception. A reader has to diff the proxy log against the ledger to notice, which is how this was found.

## 7. Suggested fix direction

Either make the call identity per call, or make the attempt axis mean what the tests say it means:

1. **Give each proxied completion its own invocation identity** (matching `direction-draft.ts:58-60`): `invocationId: \`evolve:${grant.runId}:${randomUUID()}\`` or a per-request id already available at the proxy, keeping `invocationKind: "evolve"`. The run remains addressable through the existing `runId` field (`llm-proxy.ts:269`).
2. **Or** keep the run-scoped `invocationId` and carry a per-run monotonically increasing `attemptIndex` — this needs a durable counter, so option 1 is preferable.
3. **Whichever is chosen, make the drop observable.** `store.ts:7645` should at minimum log/count a suppressed append and expose why (which key collided). A silent `return` makes a bookkeeping bug indistinguishable from correct idempotency.
4. **A regression test that pins the call, not the key**: N appends with the same run-scoped `invocationId`, distinct payloads and `attemptIndex: 0` must not collapse to one row — the counterpart to `store.test.ts:1184`, which only covers an intentional replay.

## 8. Relation to existing reports (why this is filed separately)

- **[#1109]** covers a different path and the opposite direction. It cites `services/api/src/evolution/llm-proxy.ts:245-278` as the **positive precedent** — "one `appendModelInvocationUsage` per proxied completion, keyed `invocationId: evolve:${grant.runId}`" — and uses the evolve path to argue that the native-agent path should record per turn. The word "dedup" does not appear in it, and it never claims an evolve row is dropped. This report's measurement is that the precedent it cites yields **1 row for 73 calls**, because the key the precedent reuses is also the ledger's idempotency key. Same ledger, same schema file, different defect.
- **PR #1119** (open, head `1768c9d3`) implements #1109. It changes `packages/runtime-core/src/runtime.ts`, `packages/schema/src/model-usage.ts`, `services/api/src/model-usage/index.ts` and `services/api/src/runs/index.ts`. It does **not** touch `evolution/llm-proxy.ts` or `appendModelInvocationUsage`'s guard, so this issue stands both before and after #1119 merges. If they land together, `invocationKind` will gain `delegation-track` rows and the ledger's key contract becomes load-bearing for three writers, which makes §7.3 more urgent, not less.
- **#1108** (closed by #1118), **#710/#711**, **#1125**, **#1128** were checked and share neither symptom nor root cause.
- No action on any of those issues is requested here.

## 9. Version this was measured against

- SD `main` at the time of reading: `f0efd382e5e79260386ce89674eef7af1bbc05a9` (2026-11-12T08:49:00Z).
- `services/api/src/evolution/llm-proxy.ts` blob `c447143bc7…`, 280 lines, sha256 `2f8e31af4d35db9875e52540fbe3e7cfed42389e6415f79f661d14eae85ba74e`.
- `services/api/src/store.ts` blob `baa213d4c2…`, 8132 lines, sha256 `d657e95766dd2570709ee1e9e827c525e8f1f3f60fe7da8da22b0dc376294b62`.
- Run data: existing container data volume, read-only; no agent was re-run and no model was called to produce the evidence in §5.1.

## 10. What this report does not claim

- It does not claim the run-scoped key was a mistake rather than a decision — no commit message or design note establishing intent was found, and none is asserted.
- It does not quantify historical over/under-reporting beyond the two runs above; only two Evolve runs exist on the inspected volume.
- It does not ask for backfill. The numbers for calls 2..N are not recoverable from the ledger; they exist only while the proxy log survives.
